Z||000006||BBBAD GT||05-16-2000||09:23 AM||||I'm curious what times you expect from the 3.4 on and off the bottle.  I've been throwing around the idea of a 3.4 in the future.<P>I don't want to get into a pissing contest or anything, but its rare for me (at least around here) to see a 5.0 that isn't modified someway.  Granted, the 96-98 stangs are the worst, and are easily beaten because they were just flat out dogs, with not much aftermarket to support them, but the 85-95 stangs are running pretty strong out there.    ||||reg||1
Z||000007||pollock||05-16-2000||09:35 AM||||I'm with BBADGT in that i don't want to start a pissing match (learned my lesson on an Imron paint thread a few months ago).<P>But i haven't seen any ET's posted on this forum from a 3.4 fiero, naturally aspirated or otherwise.  If you have some numbers for this, please share.  <P>Stone me, but I'm a Mustang guy, and so are most of my buddies.  The aftermarket for the 4.6s is plenty strong, and there are some FAST ones.  My buddy's 4.6 runs about a 8.5 in the 1/8 with only a dry NOS shot and exhaust.  And a 5.0 with those kind of mods is really wild.<P>Don't get me wrong.  Pretty soon i'll be ordering the HT3.4 for my Fiero.  And i've decided to add a turbo, a la Dennis LaGrua's page.  But i know what to expect.||||reg||14
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||05-16-2000||01:03 PM||||Pollock<P>Stone me too, I own a blown street Stang that just went 7.22 @ 105 mph in the 1/8 mi last weekend, with just a slick change and on pump gas.  Drove it home with a big ol smile on my face.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
